<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Exarchate of Ravenna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">584–<a href="/years/751">751</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Byzantine Exarchate of Ravenna, Exarchate of Italy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Exarchate of Ravenna was the Byzantine administration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, headed by an exarch with civil and military authority, created in the late sixth century to defend the remaining imperial territories against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>. Its lands included Ravenna, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and the Venetian lagoon, though they were gradually reduced. It ended when the Lombard king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aistulf">Aistulf</a> took Ravenna in 751.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/exarchate-of-ravenna.jpg" alt="Exarchate of Ravenna" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shuaaa2 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exarchate_of_Italy_-_600_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
